// A parser is a value: `Parser[T]` describes how to read a `T` out of text,
// and combinators build a grammar out of small ones without any of them
// knowing about the others.
//
// A refusal carries the line and column it happened at, what was found, and
// everything that would have been accepted there. A choice between two
// branches merges those expectations, so the message of a failed document
// lists every alternative at the place where the document stopped making
// sense.
//
// There is no separate lexer: a grammar reads characters, and `take_while`
// and `label` are enough to make a token layer out of them when a grammar
// wants one.
